# === Swift Package Manager ===
.build/
# `Package.resolved` is deliberately TRACKED, not ignored. Every dependency
# uses a `from:` range, so an unpinned resolve silently picks whatever is
# newest — which had already drifted between worktrees (GRDB 7.10.0 vs 7.11.1).
# This repo ships signed, notarized apps rather than a consumed library, so
# reproducibility wins: the artifact that gets notarized is the one that was
# tested. Sparkle especially, since it is embedded and signed and a bump can
# trip release.sh's DMG-growth guardrail on its own.
#
# Upgrade deliberately (`swift package update`) as its own commit, never as a
# side effect. Keep AGENTS.md's "Pinned versions" list in step.

# === Build outputs ===
build/
BrowserExtension/dist/

